            <ArticleTitle>Par(-4)oxysm in breast cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ccr.2013.06.010</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1535-6108(13)00286-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Women suffering from breast cancer often succumb to incurable recurrent disease resulting from therapy-resistant cancer cells. In this issue of Cancer Cell, Alvarez and colleagues identify downregulation of the tumor suppressor Par-4 as the key determinant in apoptosis evasion, which leads to tumor recurrence in breast cancer.</AbstractText>
